<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Ga kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1681 CE (approx.) · capital Ayawaso</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Kingdom of the Ga people around present-day Accra, which controlled coastal trade until conquered by Akwamu.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ga-speaking communities settled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accra">Accra</a> plains by the 15th century, and a kingdom formed with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayawaso">Ayawaso</a>, inland from the coast, which Europeans called Great Accra. The coastal town of Small Accra became a market for Portuguese, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, English, Danish and Swedish traders.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Ga king, the Mantse, ruled with priests of the Ga gods and town quarters. The kingdom controlled trade between the coast and the inland forest, supplying gold and slaves and buying cloth and metal goods. European companies built forts at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accra">Accra</a> in the 17th century: the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ussher-fort">Fort Crevecoeur</a>, the English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-fort">James Fort</a> and the Danish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osu-castle">Christiansborg</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The rising <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/akwamu">Akwamu</a> state attacked the Ga, destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayawaso">Ayawaso</a> in 1677 and completed its conquest by 1681. The Ga regrouped in the coastal towns, which grew into the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accra">Accra</a>, capital of independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1681 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-embl